        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A self-propelled mower that will not drive is rarely a dead mower. Work from the handle to the wheels: cable, belt, wheel gears, and only then the transmission. The first two account for most failures and cost little or nothing to fix.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Keep the deck and belt area clean, leave the cable the free play the manual asks for, and the drive should last as long as the engine. When the gearbox finally goes on an old, tired mower, that is the moment to replace it rather than repair it.
          </p>
